@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Metadata-only flaky artifacts
+
+## Design
+Replace only the GitHub annotations reader in scripts/ci/flaky_kanban.py with Actions artifacts. Leave local --report/--annotate behavior intact. No token scope changes, checks endpoint or logs fallback. Existing file_cards remains owner/dedupe authority.
+
+Each Python slice in .github/workflows/tests.yml runs a stdlib exporter after tests (!cancelled()) and uploads one pinned actions/upload-artifact artifact named flaky-metadata-v1-<run_id>-<attempt>-<slice>. Single member flaky-metadata.json, small bounded JSON. Exporter reads existing local runner report (not uploaded), discards excerpts and parameter suffixes, retaining only ASCII tests/<safe path>.py[::Class::test_function] identities (no arbitrary parameter content). Entries contain test_id, status=passed_on_retry, retried=tests|file. Strict exact-key schema includes version=1, repository, run_id, run_attempt, head_sha (event PR head or github.sha), source_sha (checkout HEAD), slice, slices, complete boolean, flaky list. Numeric ranges and sha/identity grammar are bounded. Missing/malformed local report produces complete=false and empty list, never successful empty. Source report version 1 and flaky list are mandatory. Exporter rejects unrepresentable identities rather than truncating them silently (complete=false). Parametrized cases collapse to their parent test. Runner report is only written at normal completion; no report implies incomplete.
+
+Consumer pages Actions attempt jobs and run artifacts; matches only non-skipped Python jobs whose names end in Run tests ([affected, ]N/M), requires unique slice indices and consistent M (1..64). Every expected job must have exactly one matching nonexpired artifact for this run attempt. Validate all artifact JSON and run_id/attempt/repo/head_sha/slice/slices before any card side effect. source_sha is bounded provenance, not equated to API head_sha (PR merge checkout and explicit workflow inputs differ). No test jobs means not applicable. Skipped/cancelled/unrecognized partial jobs do not mean no flakes; missing data remains unavailable and run unprocessed. Artifact absence, expired/denied access, malformed ZIP/JSON, unknown fields/version, incomplete reports log fixed FAILED/unavailable codes without payload/exception strings. Complete empty reports are processed as no flakes. Existing run/attempt dedupe remains; failed card filing retries without duplicating delivered entries.
+
+Download via canonical API /actions/artifacts/<id>/zip, authenticated only to api.github.com. Redirects to signed HTTPS object URLs drop authorization; reject other protocols and bound download size. ZIP is read in memory, never extracted; exactly one regular expected member, size/compression/encryption limits, bounded JSON. Do not trust API archive_download_url. Fixed aggregate polling receipt distinguishes complete runs/empty results from unavailable data for natural cron proof; no raw logs retrieved.
+
+### Concrete contract
+Exact schema scalar types: version integer 1 (bool rejected), repository ASCII owner/name grammar [A-Za-z0-9_.-]{1,100}/[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{1,100}, run_id and run_attempt integers 1..2^63-1, head_sha and source_sha lowercase 40-hex, slice/slices integers 1..64 with slice<=slices, complete actual boolean. flaky list <=10000 items, each exact keys test_id/status/retried; status passed_on_retry, retried tests|file. test_id <=512 ASCII chars: tests/ followed by slash-separated [A-Za-z0-9_-]+ components ending .py, optionally ::[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]* nodes. No dot traversal, parameters or whitespace. Exporter strips first [ and following text from raw node IDs before grammar validation; dedupes canonical identities. Wire JSON maximum 2 MiB, ZIP maximum 2 MiB, exactly one nonencrypted nonsymlink regular file flaky-metadata.json of maximum 2 MiB (compression ratio <=200); no additional members. Invalid data returns a fixed code, never the offending content.
+
+Consumer requires observed non-skipped Python slice indices equal 1..M, all jobs completed and not cancelled, one job per slice; any job name containing Run tests but failing anchored suffix grammar is unavailable. All-skipped Python jobs (including unexpanded matrix names with Run tests) are not_applicable, distinct from complete empty; no matching or Run tests-like jobs is also not_applicable. Cancelled runs remain unavailable and unprocessed, never no flakes: this intentionally keeps polling non-green for their lookback window because some completed slices may contain flakes, and the upload is not guaranteed. This conservative known operational cost is preferred over losing data. Newly observed means not already in processed run-attempt state, including retryable unavailable attempts. Run attempts with only a partial rerun remain unavailable (no mixing artifacts from earlier attempts). All metadata list pages are read up to 100 pages, reject overflow; list failures leave run retryable, continue other runs when possible. Completed-runs listing failure returns FAILED runs_unavailable and no state changes. No automatic binary-download retry inside the poll: transient failure is retried by next cron with run unprocessed. Two-hop API request explicitly disables redirect; signed HTTPS fetch follows no further redirects and carries no Authorization. Allowed signed destinations are *.blob.core.windows.net or *.actions.githubusercontent.com, no userinfo; reject all other hosts. Receipt: POLL complete=<n> empty=<n> unavailable=<n> not_applicable=<n>; emit only when a newly observed run exists. Per unavailable run emit FAILED run=<id>/<attempt> code=<fixed enum: jobs_unavailable|artifacts_unavailable|missing|expired|invalid|incomplete|download_unavailable>. Existing main exits 1 on FAILED. Avoid branch text from API in new artifact card path: use bounded head_sha as branch context; construct job URL from validated numeric ids/repo.
+
+Exporter CLI: python3 scripts/ci/flaky_artifact.py --report PATH --output PATH --slice N --slices M; GitHub env GITHUB_REPOSITORY, GITHUB_RUN_ID, GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT, FLAKY_HEAD_SHA supplied by workflow; source_sha via git rev-parse HEAD. Metadata failure exits nonzero; source report unavailable writes complete=false and exits zero so upload preserves explicit unavailable evidence. Upload action if !cancelled(), if-no-files-found error, retention-days 3, path only generated metadata file outside checkout. Export source report read max 16 MiB; oversize/malformed means incomplete. No mutation of runner/raw report format required.
+
+## Implementation plan
+New scripts/ci/flaky_artifact.py owns strict schema, exporter CLI and ZIP decoding/download. Existing poll_github imports helper and obtains jobs/artifact metadata through _gh, preserving API retry behavior and card delivery. Update workflow upload and exporter steps without permission changes. New tests/ci/test_flaky_artifact.py and test_flaky_artifact_poll.py exercise producer privacy, strict rejection, permission-independent ingestion, denied/missing/incomplete archives, all-or-nothing validation, pagination, duplicate/rerun mismatch, zero vs unavailable, and delivery retries. Adapt existing annotation-poll fixtures to artifact protocol; keep annotation/local tests unchanged. Run targeted suites and normal checks. Independent exact-head code review before normal PR/green exact-head CI/merge. Verify natural main CI artifacts and installed cron success using only safe aggregates; coordinate t_01a1ca20aaa3fc79. No duplicate workflow dispatch or cancellation for proof.
+
+## Code review follow-up
+Independent cumulative review deleg_7e2f726c approved with a medium card-flood concern. Consumer now rejects more than 200 aggregate flaky entries across a run before any card side effects (wire schema remains capped at 10000 per slice). Synthetic tests cover exactly 200 and 201 across slices. Explicit earlier, later or malformed job attempts fail closed; cancelled runs and incomplete reports remain FAILED/unprocessed as required, rather than the recovered WIP's terminal SKIPPED behavior. Protocol input is validated before API URL construction and all list pages are size bounded.
+
+## Source reading list
